# A BUILT-IN HANDED TO A METHOD OF LISTS IS TAKEN AS A LEAF IS. In a loop the text of the method is copied, and in the copy the built-in is called by its rows.
# `lists.every(Array.isArray)`: the question is asked in line for each element. It was a call of the text that is entered by value, which called Array.isArray by value.
# Only a built-in whose rows take no receiver, and only in a loop: outside one the call stays a call.
# declare function print(...values: unknown[]): void;
# const lists: unknown[] = [[1], [2], 3];
